module std_method_body.neg_1

// ONE seeded cause: `byte_len` is a std method whose SIGNATURE novac read and
// whose BODY it does not compile, so the call names no symbol. Every C name is
// ours (there is no foreign spelling any more), so the subset says this by
// name instead of emitting C that cannot link.
//
// The local below is the CASCADE probe, and it is the point of this fixture:
// until 2026-08-20 the gate "was anything refused?" asked the file's whole
// diagnostic count, so a refusal HERE made `@type_bind` skip its `@scope.bind`
// in `main`, and `n` came back as a second, false diagnostic -- "unknown name"
// about a name that is bound one line above.
fn width(s str) -> int => s.byte_len()

fn main() {
    ro n = 1
    println(n)
}
